    "updated_at": "2026-11-14T17:47:24Z",
    "body": "Checked by hand in the desktop app on macOS (Apple silicon), built from `main` at 4f4edcf3. The forward direction from #1520 works as \"Done means\" describes.\n\nThe setup: `examples/models/first-part.obj` imported, and a 3D Pocket whose Geometry tab has a face (the boss's top), an edge chain (one of its top edges) and a vertex (a top corner). Each row hovered with the real pointer:\n\n| Pointer on | Viewport |\n|---|---|\n| nothing (pointer elsewhere) | the selection in its normal purple style |\n| the **Face** row | the face's four sides in the thicker magenta hover style |\n| the **Chain** row | only that edge in the hover style |\n| the **Vertex** row | a magenta diamond on that corner |\n| the Chain row's **×** (remove) button | the same edge in the hover style, with the \"remove this pick\" tooltip |\n| moved off the list again | the hover style is gone: the frame is identical, pixel for pixel, to the one before hovering |\n\nScreenshots, in that order:\n\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"832\" alt=\"1-no-hover\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a0b170b5-2181-44a1-a827-8c8fece4d170\" />\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"832\" alt=\"2-hover-face-row\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4e1f5337-7ebe-4e51-9697-606742c5f226\" />\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"832\" alt=\"3-hover-chain-row\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5f8cd096-6177-466d-80b7-88107d03c367\" />\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"832\" alt=\"4-hover-vertex-row\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/760dd966-d174-4cd6-9267-eae649fdf332\" />\n<img width=\"1280\" height=\"832\" alt=\"5-hover-chain-remove-button\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d9ca216e-7b3a-416e-b2e4-9033e9ba6cd5\" />\n\nOne thing I noticed, separate from this issue: at the default window width (1280 × 832) the Geometry rows run on past the Properties panel's edge. The Face row's label is cut off (\"Face first-p…\"), and its × button can't be seen without widening the panel.\n",
